    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The runtime log confirms the new behavior end-to-end:\n- `memberId=V2NSW2616E6609E9` \u2014 the version-2 tag now lives **inside** the identifier's region code.\n- Audit event: `{\"seq\":1,...,\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` \u2014 schema version 2 with the recomputed owner segment (plain `METRO`, no V2 leak).\n- The response test passed asserting `apiVersion=2` and the nested `identity.{memberId,identityKey,householdId}` with those three gone from the top level.\n\n## What changed\n\nI released owner-identity v2 by mixing a fixed `\"V2\"` tag into each identifier's derivation, keeping every edit a tiny, self-contained change:\n\n**Identity derivation** (one line each, in the small derivation classes that own each identifier):\n- `CustomerCode.of` \u2014 the region code inside the memberId is now `\"V2\" + region` (e.g. `V2NSW\u2026`). `region(owner)` is untouched, so `locality`/`timezone`/segment stay plain.\n- `IdentityKeys.of` \u2014 hashes `\"V2|\" + \u2026`, so the key changes but equality relationships (duplicate/soft-match) are preserved.\n- `Households.idFor` \u2014 hashes `\"V2|\" + \u2026`, so household grouping is preserved.\n\nEach starts with a distinct prefix or hash input, so no v1 value can recur.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`): removed the three top-level identifier fields, added a new `OwnerIdentity` schema surfaced as a nested `identity` object plus a top-level `apiVersion: 2`. The mapper change is pure annotations (`identity.memberId`, etc.) \u2014 no new method or code body.\n\n**Audit schema** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.emit`): added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and the owner segment, both recomputed from the v2 identity. Reused the existing `OwnerSegments.of` (made public) rather than duplicating segment logic \u2014 so the segment's derived region stays plain.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged, and the segment/locality/timezone values remain the plain region code as required.",
