    "probe_text": "Here is the exact, ordered sequence of everything that fires when you `POST /api/owners` on the V1 controller (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`). I've split it into validations (each aborts the request on failure) and side-effects/transformations (each mutates state or emits something), in true execution order.\n\n## Validations (in order \u2014 each short-circuits on failure)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` on `addOwner`. Caller must have the `OWNER_ADMIN` role or the method never runs (403).\n\n2. **Bean Validation on `OwnerFieldsDto`** (`@Valid @RequestBody` + interface `@Validated`) \u2192 **400** on any failure. Fires before the method body:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words with space/`'`/`-`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`), `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Pattern` (AU/E.164), `@Size(1..25)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email`, `@DisposableEmailValidation` (rejects mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail)\n   - `address` / `addressLine1` / `addressLine2`: `@Pattern` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern` (`^[0-9]{4}$`)\n   - `registrationDate`: `@PastOrPresent`\n   - Class-level `@PostcodeValidation` (postcode must fall in the known city's range \u2014 Sydney/Melbourne/Brisbane; unknown city or null passes)\n   - Class-level `@AddressRequired` (must have a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** `address`)\n\n3. **Idempotency replay** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header; if that key was already used, returns the previously created owner with **200** and does nothing else. (Not an error \u2014 a short-circuit.)\n\n4. **Daily registration limit** \u2014 if \u2265100 non-deleted owners already share this owner's effective registration date \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n\n5. **Hard duplicate check** \u2014 `Identities.isDuplicate` (full identity key = hash of telephone + lowercased email + soundex of last name) \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**. Note: `sharesHousehold` does **not** relax this check.\n\n6. **City capacity** \u2014 if \u226550 existing owners in the same city \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n\n## Side-effects & transformations (in order)\n\nDuring DTO\u2192entity mapping, the entity setters **normalize** fields:\n- `email` \u2192 lowercased\n- `telephone` \u2192 E.164 normalized (defaults to `+61`, strips leading `0`)\n- `address`/`addressLine1`/`addressLine2` \u2192 trimmed, whitespace-collapsed, upper-cased, ST/RD/AVE expanded\n\nThen the controller computes and sets, in order:\n1. `householdId` (SHA-256 over last name + postcode)\n2. `registrationDate` \u2192 defaulted to today if null, then rolled forward off weekends/2026 holidays to a business day\n3. *(validations 4\u20136 above run here against the loaded non-deleted owner list)*\n4. `householdMemberCount` (existing housemates + 1)\n5. `membershipLevelCap` (one above max household member level)\n6. `customerCode` \u2014 assigned uniquely (`-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffixes on collision)\n7. `namesakeCount` (existing owners with same first+last name)\n8. `bulkSignupWarning` (>80 owners share the date)\n9. `capacityWarning` (\u226540 in city)\n10. `possibleDuplicateOf` (soft match: same postcode + last-name soundex but different identity; skipped when `sharesHousehold==true`)\n\nThen persistence:\n11. `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 runs `@Transactional`, delegates to `ownerRepository.save`, wrapped by a `CallMonitoringAspect` timing aspect (metrics only).\n12. `@PrePersist defaultRegistrationDate()` \u2014 sets registration date to today if still null (safety net).\n13. **DB insert.**\n14. `@PostPersist onCreate()` (via `OwnerAuditListener`), which fires three side-effects after the row exists:\n    - an **AUDIT** log line (\"owner created \u2026\")\n    - a **NOTIFY** log line (\"welcome owner \u2026\") \u2014 the welcome/notification effect\n    - `OwnerCreatedEvent.emit()` \u2014 a structured JSON `OWNER_CREATED` audit event with a monotonic sequence number (this is a log event, **not** a Spring `ApplicationEvent`)\n15. `IdempotencyKeys.remember(key, owner)` \u2014 stores the result under the Idempotency-Key.\n16. Map to `OwnerDto` (computes output-only derived fields: displayName, memberId, membershipPoints/level, segment, links, etc.), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 CREATED**.\n\nTwo things worth flagging:\n- **`sharesHousehold`** only influences the soft `possibleDuplicateOf` calculation; it does *not* relax the hard 409 identity-duplicate check. There's a `sharesHousehold`-aware `Households.isDuplicate` defined but it's unused in this path.\n- This is the **V1** controller (`/api/owners`). A separate **V2** controller serves `/api/v2/owners` \u2014 I did not include it since you asked about `/api/owners`."
